      "id": "TE-C69-axe",
      "sequence": 2280,
      "title": "గొడ్డలి (goḍḍali) — an axe",
      "headword": "గొడ్డలి",
      "romanization": "goḍḍali",
      "gloss": "an axe",
      "script": "telugu",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:2a5a36a10207f9c4",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did kaburu mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: గొడ్డలి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గొడ్డలి (goḍḍali) — \"an axe\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గొడ్డలి (goḍḍali) is an axe — an iron head on a wooden handle, for cutting a చెట్టు down or splitting firewood at the గడప."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited and old. Its first piece turns up in other Telugu words about striking, so the name says plainly what the thing does."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Asking for one is the ordinary polite request: దయచేసి, and then the word. The person hands it over handle first, and nobody throws a గొడ్డలి (goḍḍali)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గొడ్డలి (goḍḍali) is listed in DEDR's appendix of words taken from Indo-Aryan (DEDR App. 32), under Sanskrit kuṭhāra, \"axe\" (CDIAL 3244). CDIAL itself thinks kuṭhāra probably came from Dravidian, so the word may have gone north and come back. Tamil kōṭāli and Kannada koḍali are in the same appendix entry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One. Heavy, and handed over rather than thrown."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "goḍḍali",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *goḍḍali*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "dayacēsi, then goḍḍali, in that order",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *dayacēsi*, then *goḍḍali*, in that order]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say gōḍa",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *gōḍa*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "READ",
              "instruction": "శబ్దం, then say what it means",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU READ: **శబ్దం**, then say what it means]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does గొడ్డలి (goḍḍali) mean? (\"an axe\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
