      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:69a3edc8b5529e0c",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did goḍḍali mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: రంపం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రంపం (rampaṁ) — \"a saw\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రంపం (rampaṁ) is a saw. Where the గొడ్డలి (goḍḍali) breaks wood apart, the రంపం (rampaṁ) takes it apart along a line."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is a borrowing, and it came in with the trade rather than ahead of it: the long two-man saw and its name reached the carpenter's shed together."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noise is half the word. Telugu calls a rasping sound a రంపం (rampaṁ) sound, and somebody who repeats a complaint until you give way is running a రంపం (rampaṁ) over your చెవి."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రంపం (rampaṁ) is listed in DEDR's appendix of words taken from Indo-Aryan (DEDR App. 55), under Prakrit rampa, \"knife, scraper\" (CDIAL 10629), with Tamil irampam, \"a saw\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two. Both of them cut; only one cuts straight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "rampaṁ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *rampaṁ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "goḍḍali, then rampaṁ, and say which one leaves a straight edge",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *goḍḍali*, then *rampaṁ*, and say which one leaves a straight edge]"
            },
            {
